# The beads JSONL exports are NOT committed. Issues live in the local Dolt DB
# and sync over `refs/dolt/data` on the git remote, so these files are a passive
# export rather than a source of truth — nothing breaks by leaving them out.
# They are excluded because of what they CONTAIN: 590 issues carrying the
# maintainer's personal email, plus root-cause write-ups naming the private
# production host, its internal address and its real project slugs. That is
# internal project management, and this repository is public.
#
# `.beads/hooks/` stays tracked on purpose — pre-commit carries this repo's
# ruff-format gate (see CONTRIBUTING.md and the Makefile) and holds no personal
# data.
.beads/issues.jsonl
.beads/interactions.jsonl
.beads/events.jsonl

graphify-out

# Design handoff bundle from Claude Design (claude.ai/design).
# Source-of-truth mockups for the data-first redesign. Kept locally, not committed.
# Component map for agents: design/tripl/AGENTS.md
design/
# design-sync (claude.ai/design import) — generated/staged artifacts.
# Durable inputs that ARE committed: .design-sync/config.json, NOTES.md,
# conventions.md, overrides/, and frontend/.ds-entry.tsx (barrel).
# previews/ are design-handoff artifacts nothing in frontend/src imports, with
# case-only filename collisions; kept locally, not committed.
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules
.design-sync/previews/
frontend/.ds-styles.css

# Local AI-agent tooling (Claude Code, Codex, ECC, Serena). Personal to each
